course: dictionary
lesson: 3756
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, look at the words around it. That is context, and it is your best clue.
explain: «The metal flute is a woodwind too, because you blow across an edge.» Here a flute is a musical instrument, shaped like a thin tube and played by blowing across a hole near one end.
explain: Now read this: «Pour the juice into the flute and add some ice.» Juice and ice point to a tall, thin glass for drinks. Try your meaning in the sentence. If the instrument makes no sense there, the glass meaning is the right one.
fact: A flute is a musical instrument shaped like a thin tube.
fact: You play a flute by blowing across a hole near one end and pressing keys or covering holes.
fact: A flute is also a tall, thin glass used for drinks.
fact: Modern flutes are often made of metal, but they are still woodwind instruments.
fact: A flute is a woodwind because the player blows across an edge, not because of what it is made of.
exercise: «Flute lessons start on Tuesday after school.» What is a flute here? | * A musical instrument | A kind of sweet | A type of bird | A tall, thin glass
exercise: Ruby says, «Pass me the flute, please.» The table has a jug of lemonade and a tray of cups. What does flute mean here? | A flat plate for cakes | A wooden spoon | A musical instrument played by blowing | * A tall, thin glass used for drinks
exercise: «The shiny metal flute is a woodwind because the player blows across an edge.» What makes the flute a woodwind? | * How the sound is made, by blowing across an edge | Its colour, which is shiny | Its size, which is small | What it is made of, which is metal
test: In a cartoon, a snake charmer plays a flute to a cobra. What is the flute here? | A kind of hat | * A musical instrument played by blowing | A type of snake | A tall, thin glass for drinks
test: Why is a metal flute counted as a woodwind? | Because it is made of wood | Because it is shaped like a thin tube only | * Because the player blows across an edge to make the sound | Because it is shiny
exam: Ellie reads, «The flute stood on the table, full of cold lemonade.» Which meaning fits best? | A kind of bird | A musical instrument played by blowing | A large bowl for soup | * A tall, thin glass for drinks
